{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V5b7FRQuxgofLCq6LVX5Pj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Export pipeline\n\nThis page describes what happens to an export request.\n\n## Request\n\nWhen an export is requested, the payload is validated. Requests above 100,000 rows are\nrejected. If the payload is valid, a job is enqueued and a `202` is returned.\n\n## Processing\n\nThe job is picked up and the CSV file is generated. The file is encrypted before it is\nuploaded to the bucket. If something goes wrong, the job is retried up to three times,\nafter which it is moved to the dead-letter queue.\n\n## Delivery\n\nOnce the upload is done, a download link is sent by email. The link is expired after\n24 hours.\n\n## Backups\n\nBackups of the bucket are rotated weekly.\nimport json\nimport os\n\nimport pika\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\n\napp = FastAPI()\nMAX_ROWS = 100_000\n\n\ndef validate_payload(payload: dict) -> None:\n    if \"account_id\" not in payload:\n        raise HTTPException(422, \"account_id is required\")\n    if payload.get(\"rows\", 0) > MAX_ROWS:\n        raise HTTPException(413, f\"exports above {MAX_ROWS} rows are not supported\")\n\n\n@app.post(\"/exports\", status_code=202)\ndef create_export(payload: dict) -> dict:\n    validate_payload(payload)\n    connection = pika.BlockingConnection(pika.URLParameters(os.environ[\"QUEUE_URL\"]))\n    channel = connection.channel()\n    channel.basic_publish(exchange=\"\", routing_key=\"exports\", body=json.dumps(payload))\n    connection.close()\n    return {\"status\": \"queued\"}\ndeploy:\nalerts.yaml\n\ndocs:\npipeline.md\n\nscripts:\nrequeue_dead.py\ndocs/pipeline.md:7:When an export is requested, the payload is validated. Requests above 100,000 rows are\nscripts/requeue_dead.py:4:    uv run python scripts/requeue_dead.py --limit 50   move at most 50 messages\nscripts/requeue_dead.py:15:    parser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=100)\nscripts/requeue_dead.py:21:    while moved < args.limit:\nexporter/worker.py:14:    rows = [f\"{job['account_id']},{n}\" for n in range(job.get(\"rows\", 0))]\nexporter/worker.py:15:    return \"\\n\".join(rows).encode()\nexporter/gateway.py:8:MAX_ROWS = 100_000\nexporter/gateway.py:14:    if payload.get(\"rows\", 0) > MAX_ROWS:\nexporter/gateway.py:15:        raise HTTPException(413, f\"exports above {MAX_ROWS} rows are not supported\")","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88b92149-f431-4ae8-a1fd-2331e62f59b8","uuid":"24e88de5-982d-481e-9df3-d74768644afd","timestamp":"2026-11-22T22:16:29.752Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Export pipeline\n\nThis page describes what happens to an export request.\n\n## Request\n\nWhen an export is requested, the payload is validated. Requests above 100,000 rows are\nrejected. If the payload is valid, a job is enqueued and a `202` is returned.\n\n## Processing\n\nThe job is picked up and the CSV file is generated. The file is encrypted before it is\nuploaded to the bucket. If something goes wrong, the job is retried up to three times,\nafter which it is moved to the dead-letter queue.\n\n## Delivery\n\nOnce the upload is done, a download link is sent by email. The link is expired after\n24 hours.\n\n## Backups\n\nBackups of the bucket are rotated weekly.\nimport json\nimport os\n\nimport pika\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\n\napp = FastAPI()\nMAX_ROWS = 100_000\n\n\ndef validate_payload(payload: dict) -> None:\n    if \"account_id\" not in payload:\n        raise HTTPException(422, \"account_id is required\")\n    if payload.get(\"rows\", 0) > MAX_ROWS:\n        raise HTTPException(413, f\"exports above {MAX_ROWS} rows are not supported\")\n\n\n@app.post(\"/exports\", status_code=202)\ndef create_export(payload: dict) -> dict:\n    validate_payload(payload)\n    connection = pika.BlockingConnection(pika.URLParameters(os.environ[\"QUEUE_URL\"]))\n    channel = connection.channel()\n    channel.basic_publish(exchange=\"\", routing_key=\"exports\", body=json.dumps(payload))\n    connection.close()\n    return {\"status\": \"queued\"}\ndeploy:\nalerts.yaml\n\ndocs:\npipeline.md\n\nscripts:\nrequeue_dead.py\ndocs/pipeline.md:7:When an export is requested, the payload is validated. Requests above 100,000 rows are\nscripts/requeue_dead.py:4:    uv run python scripts/requeue_dead.py --limit 50   move at most 50 messages\nscripts/requeue_dead.py:15:    parser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=100)\nscripts/requeue_dead.py:21:    while moved < args.limit:\nexporter/worker.py:14:    rows = [f\"{job['account_id']},{n}\" for n in range(job.get(\"rows\", 0))]\nexporter/worker.py:15:    return \"\\n\".join(rows).encode()\nexporter/gateway.py:8:MAX_ROWS = 100_000\nexporter/gateway.py:14:    if payload.get(\"rows\", 0) > MAX_ROWS:\nexporter/gateway.py:15:        raise HTTPException(413, f\"exports above {MAX_ROWS} rows are not supported\")","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01V5b7FRQuxgofLCq6LVX5Pj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
